# Code Consistency

## Choose the applicable convention

1. Follow explicit project rules and the configured language/runtime constraints.
2. Follow a documented modernization direction when the project is migrating.
3. Otherwise, match the established style of the module being edited.

Use the project's actual formatter and linter configuration. Avoid imposing a
new naming, import, quoting, typing, or file-layout preference simply because
it is common in another project.

## Keep edits focused

- Limit formatting changes to the affected code. Keep unrelated cleanup out of
  the feature or fix so its behavior is straightforward to review.
- Preserve deliberate conventions in vendored or generated code; use the
  existing update mechanism when one is provided.
- Keep comments for non-obvious logic, constraints, or reasons. Avoid comments
  and documentation blocks that merely narrate the implementation.
- Choose asynchronous control flow for clarity and keep it consistent within
  one operation.

Run the applicable project checks. Fix the cause of a finding rather than
weakening validation merely to make the change pass.
